@startuml Airports-SD-BusiestAirports
autonumber
title Busiest airports by number of routes — GET /api/airports/statistics/busiest (US210, contract B5)
actor "Backoffice Operator" as BO
participant "airports-1\n: AirportController" as Ctrl
participant ": AirportStatisticsService" as Service
participant ": FlightRoutesClient" as Client
participant ": ReplicatedServiceClient" as Rep
participant "Flight Routes\n(any replica)" as FR
participant ": AirportReplicaQueries" as Queries

activate BO
BO -> Ctrl : GET /api/airports/statistics/busiest?limit=3
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Service : busiestAirports(3)
activate Service
Service -> Client : routeCountsByAirport()
activate Client
Client -> Rep : call(GET /api/routes/statistics/count-by-airport)
Rep -> FR : GET (round-robin; failover to the next replica)
FR -> FR : sums the counts of ALL its replicas
FR --> Rep : 200 {"LIS":3, "MAD":3, "OPO":2, "CDG":2, ...}
Rep --> Client : Map<String, Long>
deactivate Client
note right of Rep
  401/403 → same status.
  No Flight Routes replica answers → 503.
end note
Service -> Service : sort by count desc, then IATA;\nkeep top 3
loop for each IATA of the top 3
    Service -> Queries : findByIata(iata)
    Queries --> Service : AirportDTO (local or from a peer)
end
note right of Service
  Lookup by IATA (allowed to Backoffice Operator),
  not the US108 search (ATCC only): the user's JWT
  is forwarded to the peers, which apply the same rules.
end note
Service --> Ctrl : [rank 1 LIS 3, rank 2 MAD 3, rank 3 CDG 2]
deactivate Service
Ctrl --> BO : 200 List<BusiestAirportDTO>
deactivate Ctrl
@enduml
